From 3ee0d3d4b24f733cb0ae558e0a54f62387781765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] dt-bindings: pwm: add hi3716cv200 pwm

The Hi3716CV200 carries the same PMOC block: three outputs at the same
offsets, feeding its CPU, core and GPU rails in that order. Give it its
own compatible value, as the output count is what each part brings to
the block.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml     | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm.yaml
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@ description:
   of outputs differs between the SoCs carrying this block, so each SoC has
   its own compatible value. The Hi3798MV100 carries the same block, whose
   three outputs sit at the same offsets and feed its core, CPU and GPU rails.
+  The Hi3716CV200 carries the same block, whose three outputs feed its CPU,
+  core and GPU rails.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: pwm.yaml#
@@ -25,6 +27,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - hisilicon,hi3798cv200-pwm
       - hisilicon,hi3798mv100-pwm
+      - hisilicon,hi3716cv200-pwm
 
   reg:
     description:
